## Correct the duplicate rule

The accepted [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone.
The executable examples below contradict that shortcut: identical subjects can describe different
causes, and different subjects can describe the same cause. Missing tenant information does not
establish a match. Keep such reports unplaced until there is enough evidence.

<DedupeExplorer />

The [replacement decision proposal](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) records the correction
without rewriting the accepted historical decision. Reviewers should merge reports only when the
underlying failure agrees, using the report body, tenant locale, form version, channel and reproduction.
Do not infer a new cause from a subject or an intake tag alone.

## Follow-up and verification

- Preserve separate parser and hint dispositions, including report-ID membership in the repository's evidence file.
- Keep the desk-note exceptions visible until reproduced; do not count them twice or silently discard their wording.
- Refresh the export before making claims about the live queue; recompute rather than manually adjusting totals.
- Distinguish the desk's reported parser fix from independent verification; the form hint was retired, not fixed.
- Re-review the old triage advice and its replacement decision with the support owner.

